// Speaker Idrenne, crane, the Windreach Clans (bible 3.6, 4.5, 8.5; character-bibles.md §8). The Moving Camp:
// three nights at three sites, the camp moving on between them (PRG-21): the fire ring (Camp_2), the riverbed
// (River_2), the high grass (Fire_1). The Wind Gate's leap falls between the second night and the third.
// Voice: amused, unhurried; answers with where she was standing when she learned the answer. Does not say "always"
// or "never": the clans live in the particular.

title: Camp_Idrenne
---
<<if flag("windreach.camp.night") >= 1>>
    <<if has_flag("keystone.windreach")>>
        Idrenne: We cook on a flat rock from the river now. The soup hasn't noticed.
    <<elseif has_flag("windreach.camp.walked")>>
        Idrenne: You're known here. Sit anywhere. Everyone does.
    <<elseif camp_site() == 0>>
        Idrenne: We walk at first light. There's a bedroll by the wagons, if you're coming.
    <<elseif flag("windreach.camp.night") >= 2>>
        Idrenne: The camp's on the high grass tonight, past the Gate. Only the post-wagon stays.
    <<else>>
        Idrenne: The camp's gone on to the riverbed. Follow the grass we flattened, east.
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: You came down the south road from the Plateau.
Idrenne: I was standing by the first stone when I learned what that means. A map in the pack. A question.
Idrenne: Sit. Eat first. Questions keep.
-> Isolde Marr named you. One of five.
    Idrenne: Isolde. I was knee-deep in the Dry River when she asked me the same thing.
    Idrenne: I told her to walk with us. She said she'd come back. Here you are instead.
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> Is anyone out here hunting you?
    Idrenne: Hunting, no. Counting, maybe. A bird with a brass lens, a day behind us.
    Idrenne: I learned that at the ninth stone, watching grass bend where no wind was.
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> ...
    Idrenne: Good. The grass talks enough for both of us.
    <<voice drift windreach>>
Idrenne: We walk tomorrow. Three days, three fires. Walk with us, and ask your question at the last one.
<<flag windreach.idrenne.met 1>>
<<flag windreach.camp.night 1>>
===

title: River_Idrenne_Night
---
<<if flag("windreach.camp.night") < 1>>
    Riverbed: Cold ashes in a ring of boats. Somebody camps here, some nights.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if flag("windreach.camp.night") >= 2>>
    Idrenne: The fourth stone is the riverbed. We sat on it. Not many maps can say that.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: Second fire. Your feet will hate you tomorrow. Mine did, the year I learned this walk.
Idrenne: You looked at the stones. Nine of them. The Guild thinks they're a boundary.
Idrenne: They're a map. Eight are places we stop: the Long Grass, the river, the Gate, the high grass.
Idrenne: The fire, the star, the old sea road, the south gate of your Plateau.
Idrenne: The ninth has nothing carved on it. The ninth is wherever we're standing.
-> A map nobody can take away.
    Idrenne: Somebody's trying. The lens bird sights them one by one. I watched him from the reeds.
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> Show me the one he's sighting.
    Idrenne: The ninth, at dusk. He's sighting the one that can't be sighted. Let him learn that.
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> Then the ninth stone is here.
    Idrenne: Tonight it is. Tomorrow it's the Gate. You're quick. I was slower, and older.
    <<voice drift windreach>>
Idrenne: Tomorrow is the Wind Gate. The young jump. Nobody's come up the updraft in forty years.
Idrenne: We sing them off anyway. Somebody might.
<<flag windreach.stones.named 1>>
<<flag windreach.camp.night 2>>
===

title: Grass_Idrenne_Night
---
<<if not has_flag("windreach.leap.done")>>
    Grass: Grass over her head, trampled flat in a circle. The clan camps here past the Gate.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("windreach.camp.walked")>>
    Idrenne: The third fire's ash. Mine's up the rise, if you've a question left.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: Third fire. On the last night we say where we were standing when we learned something.
Ossa: In the riverbed. I learned a boat doesn't need water to be a boat.
Brek: At the Gate, forty-one years back. I learned I couldn't fly. Tonight I learned somebody still can.
Idrenne: Your turn, map-bird. Where were you standing?
-> At the Edge, when Isolde walked in.
    Idrenne: Then that one's yours. Say it again next year and it's ours too.
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> Here. With all of you.
    Idrenne: Ha. That's a cheat. It's a good cheat. We'll allow it.
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> On a stone that isn't carved.
    Idrenne: The ninth. You were listening. Brek, she was listening.
    <<voice drift windreach>>
Idrenne: There. Now you're known here. That's all it is. Everyone walks it, and everyone's known.
Idrenne: The Guild wanted paper and a stone in a vault. We have legs and names.
<<flag windreach.camp.night 3>>
<<flag windreach.camp.walked 1>>
===
